  "findings": [
    "The four Bill root fixing meshes are byte-signature unchanged across V8, Bill-section V2, and paired-bill V2. Each fastener is fully classified inside the closed evaluated Profiled upper bill blade 0 in all three sources: all vertices, face centers and centers are odd/even inside; pin/blade BVH surface-pair candidates are zero. Thus these parts are buried/occluded, not floating in exterior air. Sampled nearest blade-surface separation increases from 5.57\u20136.06 mm in V8 to 12.22\u201313.15 mm in Bill-section V2 and remains there in paired-bill V2. This suggests the section study deepens burial of the inherited root-fixing caps; owner intent should decide whether these are deliberately internal anchors or are meant to be externally visible fasteners.",
    "Anatomical left is +X and anatomical right is -X. The fixing objects\u2019 local X basis is exactly world/native X, and the matching blade side-wall normal is nearly \u00b1X (paired study dot 0.990\u20130.997). The objects are near-isotropic small closed heads rather than elongated shafts. Rays along signed outward X from their vertex-average centers hit the blade wall 15.64\u201316.00 mm away in paired V2, versus 12.03\u201312.18 mm in V8. Therefore \u00b1X is the appropriate direction for any later reseating study; these numbers measure how deeply centers sit inside the blade, not an exterior gap.",
    "The paired study itself leaves the stationary root fixing/support components unchanged. Its root-area stationary plate junctions are mixed: blade 0 to blade 1 has a 1.08 mm sampled seam (2.03 mm in V8 and Bill-section V2), with no BVH candidates; blade 0 to Overlapping nasal hood is about 0.02 mm with 58 broad-phase face candidates; blade 0 to each Cere root transition is about 0.001 mm with 35 candidates per side in both section-study variants, versus 5.59 mm and no candidates in V8. The latter interfaces are plausibly lapped/near-seated, but broad-phase candidates do not establish strict crossing or exclude coplanarity.",
    "Overlapping nasal hood to each Cere root transition remains 0.84\u20130.88 mm sampled separation with no BVH candidates through the chain. This is a possible fine panel seam, not a proven defect. Nasal hood fixing samples are coincident/overlapping with the hood surface at sampled resolution (0\u20130.12 mm; 10\u201312 broad-phase candidates), consistent with that fastener family being seated at its named host, subject to the same sampling limits."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Distances are finite samples against actual evaluated triangle surfaces, not exhaustive closest-feature calculations.",
    "BVH candidate counts are not proper crossing classifications; no strict crossing, coplanar overlap, containment, or penetration depth claim is made.",
    "Static native rest geometry only. No full-head clearance, jaw motion, force, manufacturing tolerance, owner acceptance or publication claim.",
    "Containment is sampled odd/even parity on a closed target mesh plus no BVH surface-pair candidates; it strongly supports burial but is not a volumetric Boolean proof for every point of the fastener solids."
  ],
